      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s early economy boasted seven sawmills, two chair factories, a pail factory, a children’s carriage factory, and a bit‑brace factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erving%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In one year, Erving’s dense forests supplied as many as 1,495,000 railroad ties and telegraph poles.",
